cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this theoretical model, CAD geometry, PCB netlist generator, C99 firmware, or FPGA RTL in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Sub-Harmonic Injection Locking and Gyrotropic Parity Symmetry Breaking in a Low-Pressure Argon Standing-Wave RF Cavity Processor"
type: software
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-17"
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
  - family-names: "Grimm"
    given-names: "Justin D."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5299-0243"
    affiliation: "Independent Dandelion Substrate Research Group, Gurley, Alabama 35748, USA"
abstract: >-
  Archival compuscript and closed-loop hardware-software specification (v1.1.0)
  for a partial-vacuum Argon RF standing-wave balanced-ternary processor
  operating on the spherical TM101 mode at 915.0 MHz with 2.745 GHz third-harmonic
  injection locking, 104.0 Hz modulo-13 Am-241 Erlang timing, 28.0 mT Co-60
  gyrotropic D3-to-C3 symmetry breaking, OpenSCAD-to-C99 Q2.14 phase-trim
  tables, 13-channel homodyne KiCad netlist synthesis, and Lattice iCE40HX8K
  single-cycle ternary arbitration.
keywords:
  - standing-wave computing
  - balanced ternary logic
  - sub-harmonic injection locking
  - Kuramoto-Sakaguchi dynamics
  - cold-plasma gyrotropy
  - Ramsauer-Townsend minimum
  - Lattice iCE40HX8K FPGA
  - deterministic hardware verification
